#!name=GFW Optimized Proxy List (CN) 2026
#!desc=Proxy list for getting past the Great Firewall in mainland China, blacklist mode (only what is blocked goes through the proxy). Covers Google/Alphabet (Search, Gmail, Drive, Docs, Meet, Maps, Photos, YouTube, Play, Android, Firebase, GCP, Gemini), Meta (Facebook, Instagram, Threads, Messenger, WhatsApp, Oculus), Telegram, Viber, TikTok, X/Twitter, LINE/KakaoTalk/Naver, AI, dev, media/streaming, international press, public DNS, plus IP-CIDR (checked against BGP, 09/2026) for services whose DNS gets poisoned. Every entry is measured from inside China (Globalping, OONI, itdog); sites that open directly stay out. 2026-10-04: +Bluesky, APKMirror/APKPure/F-Droid, Binance/Coinbase/TradingView, VOA Chinese (0/6 China probes on Telecom/Unicom/Mobile).
#!homepage=https://github.com/kulinh/gfw-vnm

# ============================================================================
#  HOW TO USE (blacklist mode, while in China)
#  1) Settings > Modules: add this module.
#  2) In your config (.conf) the LAST line of [Rule] must be:
#        FINAL,DIRECT
#     => the domains below go through PROXY, everything else goes direct.
#  3) If a mainland app (banks, State Grid ...) complains it detects a proxy:
#        Settings > Proxy > change the proxy type from HTTP to none (TUN mode).
#  Note: module rules win over config rules, and a module higher in the list
#  wins over one below it. To override, put a small module of your own on top.
#  4) cf-vpn panel configs (RWL-CN) already INLINE every rule of this file
#     (the Worker fetches it when it builds the config): no need to add the
#     module there; every rule points at the config's PROXY group.
#     Add the module only to a config you wrote yourself.
#     RULE-SET version (no policy): sr_proxy_list_CN.list; sing-box / Hiddify:
#     sing-box/sr_proxy_list_CN.srs (both generated by tools/build.py).
#  Sources (09/2026): gfwlist, gstatic.com/ipranges/goog.json,
#  RIPEstat announced-prefixes AS32934 (Meta), AS62014/62041/59930/44907/211157
#  (Telegram).
# ============================================================================

[Rule]

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GOOGLE / ALPHABET (the whole ecosystem)
#   *.google.com already covers accounts, drive, docs, sheets, slides, meet,
#   photos, maps, mail, play, news, translate, calendar, chat, gemini, store...
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
